---
layout: base.njk
title: Compare
permalink: /compare/
description: Atomdrift Scan vs. VirusTotal, Socket, Aikido, SafeDep and ClamAV on live zero-day supply-chain malware. Measured daily on an identical cohort, every sample published. Local, Apache-2.0, built to be embedded.
---

<style>
  .compare { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4px 24px 64px; }

  /* one bar palette for every engine: hostile solid, suspicious pale, grey = unreadable.
     Atomdrift is marked by its label, not by a colour of its own. */
  :root {
    --h: #9abe25; --s: #cfe09a; --na: #dfe3e8; --e: #d64545;
    --t-hostile: #dc2626; --t-suspicious: #e0a526; --t-benign: #2f9e63; --t-nodata: #7b8494;
  }

  /* ---------- hero ---------- */
  /* Keep the proof card compact: at the full page width this makes it about 30%
     narrower than the old 1.45fr/1fr split and gives the badge row one clean line. */
  .cmp-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(240px, 28.5%); gap: 28px;
              align-items: start; padding: 18px 0 4px; }
  /* No hard break: a <br> splits at the same word whatever the column width, which
     is why it read as arbitrary. balance lets the browser even out the lines itself. */
  .cmp-hero h1 { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: 2.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--carbon);
                 letter-spacing: -1.1px; line-height: 1.03; margin: 0; text-wrap: balance; }
  .cmp-hero h1 em { display: block; font-style: normal; color: var(--atomdrift-blue); font-size: 1.3rem;
                    font-weight: 700; margin-top: 8px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .cmp-hero .say { margin: 12px 0 0; color: var(--iron); line-height: 1.6; font-size: .95rem; }
  .cmp-hero .say b { color: var(--carbon); font-weight: 600; }
  .instl { margin-top: 16px; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .84rem; background: var(--carbon);
           border-radius: 7px; padding: 11px 14px; color: var(--toxic); overflow-x: auto; }
  .facts { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--slate); }

  /* Our own two numbers, not a face-off. The comparison lives in the leaderboard
     directly below; repeating it here cost width the headline column needed. */
  .proof { background: var(--carbon); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px; color: #fff;
           display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .proof .scores { display: flex; gap: 26px; }
  .proof .n { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: 2.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: .85;
              letter-spacing: -2px; color: var(--toxic); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .proof .n.fp { color: #fff; }
  .proof .l { font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .09em; color: #b9bfc9; margin-top: 8px;
              text-transform: uppercase; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  /* The span the two numbers pool over, read before the numbers themselves. */
  .proof .l.win { margin-top: 0; }
  .proof .at { font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .72rem; color: #d5d9d2;
               border-top: 1px solid #2a2e28; padding-top: 11px; }
  .proof .at b { color: var(--toxic); font-weight: 700; }
  .proof .dial { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }
  .proof .dial-label { color: #d5d9d2; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .7rem;
                       font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .proof input[type=range] { -webkit-appearance: none; appearance: none; width: 100%; background: transparent;
                             height: 44px; margin: 0; cursor: ew-resize; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-runnable-track { height: 3px; border-radius: 2px; background: #71787f; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-moz-range-track { height: 3px; border-radius: 2px; background: #71787f; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-thumb { -webkit-appearance: none; width: 20px; height: 20px;
    border-radius: 50%; background: var(--toxic); margin-top: -8.5px; transition: transform .12s ease; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-moz-range-thumb { width: 20px; height: 20px; border: 0; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--toxic); transition: transform .12s ease; }
  .proof input[type=range]:hover::-webkit-slider-thumb { transform: scale(1.25); }
  .proof input[type=range]:hover::-moz-range-thumb { transform: scale(1.25); }
  .proof input[type=range]:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--toxic); outline-offset: 5px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .proof .ends { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace;
                 font-size: .68rem; color: #b9bfc9; }
  .proof p { margin: 0; font-size: .74rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #b9bfc9; }
  .proof p b { color: #eef0f3; font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---------- sections ---------- */
  .compare h2 { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--carbon);
                border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: 6px; margin: 40px 0 4px; letter-spacing: -.3px;
                display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 9px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .compare h2 .note, details.appendix > summary .note { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 400; color: var(--slate); }
  /* The ecosystem dropdown sits at the right of its heading, in the note's voice. */
  .compare h2 .eco-pick { margin-left: auto; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: .74rem; font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--iron); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .compare h2 .eco-pick select { font: inherit; color: var(--carbon); background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px; padding: 3px 6px; min-height: 28px; }
  .legend small { font-size: inherit; color: var(--slate); }
  /* Page-level copy should use the content width. The hero's grid already gives
     its copy a readable measure; another max-width here only creates a ragged,
     half-empty column below full-width charts. */
  .compare .sub { color: var(--iron); font-size: .88rem; margin: 10px 0 14px; }
  .compare .sub b { color: var(--carbon); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---------- bars ---------- */
  .rows { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr max-content; gap: 6px 12px; align-items: center; margin: 12px 0 8px; }
  .rows .rn { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: .8rem; white-space: nowrap; color: var(--graphite); }
  .rows .rn.us { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); font-weight: 800; }
  .rows .tr { height: 17px; background: var(--mist); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; display: flex;
              box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,.05); }
  .rows .hb, .legend .hostile-key { background: var(--h); }
  .rows .hb, .rows .sb, .rows .un { height: 100%; }
  .rows .sb, .legend .suspicious-key { background-color: var(--s);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(0,0,0,.18) 0 2px, transparent 2px 5px); }
  .rows .un, .legend .unsupported-key { background-color: var(--na);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0,0,0,.2) 0 1px, transparent 1px 4px); }
  .rows .eb, .legend .errored-key { background: var(--e); }
  /* One failure in a hundred is a sub-pixel sliver of bar, which is a tooltip
     nobody can land on; 5px keeps it aimable without reading as a real share. */
  .rows .eb { height: 100%; min-width: 5px; cursor: help; }
  /* Grey (scope) and red (failure) anchor right, in that order; whichever comes
     first takes the auto margin so the pair hugs the right edge either way. */
  .rows .un, .rows .sb + .eb, .rows .hb + .eb, .rows .eb:first-child { margin-left: auto; }
  .rows .un + .eb { margin-left: 0; }
  .rows .rv { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: .8rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
              text-align: right; min-width: 36px; color: var(--carbon); }
  /* The range to the loosest setting: secondary to the counted number. */
  .rows .rv .rs { font-weight: 500; color: var(--slate); white-space: nowrap; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .rows .rv { max-width: 7.5rem; }
    .rows .rv .rs { display: block; font-size: .66rem; white-space: normal; line-height: 1.3; }
  }
  .legend { display: flex; gap: 8px 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; font-size: .72rem; color: var(--iron); }
  .legend i { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 2px; display: inline-block; margin-right: 5px; vertical-align: -1px; }
  .fig-note { color: var(--slate); font-size: .74rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .fig-note b { color: var(--graphite); }
  .fig-note a { color: var(--slate); }
  .fig-note code { white-space: nowrap; }
  .q-none { margin: 14px 0 4px; font-size: .84rem; }
  .lnk { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; white-space: nowrap; }

  /* ---------- frontier ---------- */
  .frontier-wrap { margin: 14px 0 4px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .frontier-wrap svg { width: 100%; min-width: 720px; height: auto; display: block; }
  .q-grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  /* Solid hairlines throughout: a dashed rule reads as "projection" or "threshold"
     when it is only ever a grid or a divider. */
  .q-axis, .q-div { stroke: #c9ccd1; stroke-width: 1; }
  .q-tick { fill: var(--slate); font-size: 10.5px; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .q-head { fill: var(--carbon); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif;
            letter-spacing: -.4px; }
  .q-headsub { fill: var(--iron); font-size: 13px; font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .q-alab { fill: var(--carbon); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .q-asub { fill: var(--slate); font-size: 10.5px; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .q-target { fill: #2a78d6; opacity: .07; }
  .q-target-edge { fill: none; stroke: #bcd8f2; stroke-width: 1; }
  .q-quad { fill: #1e6bb8; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .08em;
            font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .q-pt { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 2; }
  /* Solid, because it is a measured frontier rather than "anywhere along here";
     the gradient tail marks where the budget starts costing something. */
  /* An engine's other settings: grey, quiet, and selectable. The selected one is
     the coloured point; its grey dot gets a ring so the choice stays visible. */
  .q-line { fill: none; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linejoin: round; opacity: .5; }
  .q-opt { stroke-width: 0; opacity: .5; cursor: pointer; }
  .q-opt:hover, .q-opt:focus-visible { opacity: .9; outline: none; }
  .q-opt.on { fill: #fff; stroke-width: 2; opacity: 1; }
  /* Label leaders: darker and finer than any setting line, so neither is mistaken
     for the other. */
  .q-leader { stroke: #6b7280; stroke-width: .75; }
  /* One slider per engine with settings to choose from. */
  .q-tune { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 8px 22px; margin: 6px 0 4px; }
  .q-knob { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 2px 10px; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--iron); }
  .q-kname { font-weight: 700; color: var(--carbon); }
  .q-kname::before { content: ""; display: inline-block; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--c); margin-right: 6px; }
  .q-knob input { width: 100%; accent-color: var(--carbon); min-height: 28px; }
  .q-kval { grid-column: 2; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .q-kval b { font-weight: 600; color: var(--slate); margin-right: 4px; }
  /* One label format for every engine: bold name, plain rates, grey setting. */
  .q-lab { font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif; fill: var(--iron);
           /* A halo in the page colour, so no line or grid ever runs through text. */
           paint-order: stroke; stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 3.5px; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .q-lname { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--carbon); }
  .q-setting { fill: var(--slate); }
  /* Outline rings so a coincident rival dot stays visible inside them. */
  /* The axis break: a surface-coloured stroke under a hairline, so the two slashes
     read as a cut in the axis rather than as marks floating beside it. */
  .q-break-mask { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 5; }
  .q-break { stroke: #c9ccd1; stroke-width: 1; }

  /* ---------- the difference matrix ---------- */
  /* Three rows, two columns: the least text that still makes a comparison. Each
     cell is one sentence, so the whole argument is scannable in a column sweep. */
  .diffs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .diffs > div { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e3e6ea; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px;
                 font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--iron); }
  /* Three tiers, top to bottom: the claims in the site's green (same tint as the
     old "us" cells and the sponsor box), the how in white, the fit in the nav's grey. */
  .diffs > div:nth-child(-n+3) { background: var(--toxic-dim); border-color: var(--toxic-muted); }
  .diffs > div:nth-child(n+7) { background: var(--mist); border-color: var(--border); }
  .diffs b { display: block; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .92rem; font-weight: 800;
             color: var(--carbon); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .diffs code { font-size: .78rem; }
  .vs { margin-top: 16px; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--iron); }
  .vs b { color: var(--carbon); font-weight: 650; }

  /* ---------- trend ---------- */
  .trend-wrap { position: relative; height: 340px; margin-top: 10px; }

  /* ---------- false positives ---------- */
  table.fpt { border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 12px; font-size: .8rem; }
  table.fpt th, table.fpt td { text-align: left; padding: 7px 14px 7px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
                               vertical-align: top; }
  table.fpt thead th { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .66rem; letter-spacing: .07em;
                       text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slate); font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
  table.fpt td:first-child { font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 600;
                             color: var(--graphite); white-space: nowrap; }
  table.fpt a { font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .76rem; text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; word-break: break-all; }
  table.fpt a.fphostile { color: var(--h); }
  table.fpt a.fpsuspicious { color: var(--toxic-dark); }
  table.fpt a:hover { background: var(--cream); }

  /* ---------- samples + method ---------- */
  /* Folded by default: it is the evidence, not the argument. Anyone who wants to
     check the work opens it; nobody else has to scroll past 43 filenames. */
  details.appendix { margin-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 6px; }
  details.appendix > summary { cursor: pointer; list-style: none; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 9px;
    flex-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--carbon);
    min-height: 44px; padding: 8px 0; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  details.appendix > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  details.appendix > summary::before { content: "▸"; color: var(--toxic-dark); font-size: .8rem; transition: transform .15s ease; }
  details.appendix[open] > summary::before { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  details.appendix > summary:hover { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); }
  details.appendix > summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--atomdrift-blue); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 3px; }
  .samples { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2px 22px; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace;
             font-size: .74rem; margin-top: 10px; }
  .samples a { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden;
               text-overflow: ellipsis; display: flex; align-items: center; min-height: 28px; }
  .samples a::before { content: "▪ "; color: var(--h); }
  .samples a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .meth { background: var(--cream); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 15px;
          font-size: .78rem; color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.65; margin-top: 14px; }
  .meth b { color: var(--carbon); font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .who { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .who > div { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e3e6ea; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; }
  /* Same tiers as the cards above, left to right: the primary audience in green,
     then white, then grey. */
  .who > div:first-child { background: var(--toxic-dim); border-color: var(--toxic-muted); }
  .who > div:last-child { background: var(--mist); border-color: var(--border); }
  .who h3 { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .92rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--carbon);
            letter-spacing: -.2px; margin: 0 0 7px; }
  .who p { margin: 0; font-size: .82rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--iron); }
  /* isotope13's own palette (fuschia on its mist), so the sponsor line reads as theirs, not ours. */
  .hosted { margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: .84rem; font-weight: 600;
            background: #fdf5fc; border: 1px solid #FF00CC; color: #CC0077; }
  .hosted a { color: #CC0077; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline;
              text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .closer { margin-top: 34px; background: var(--carbon); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 24px; display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .closer h3 { color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -.5px; margin: 0; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; }
  .closer p { margin: 5px 0 0; color: #b9bfc9; font-size: .78rem; }
  .closer .inst { font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .78rem; background: #1c1f1a; color: var(--toxic);
                  border-radius: 7px; padding: 10px 15px; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .cmp-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
    .samples { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .cmp-hero h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; }
    .samples a { min-height: 44px; }
    /* The scatter needs 720px to be legible; narrower than that it would scroll
       sideways with Atomdrift's own mark off-screen. The sliders carry the same
       numbers and fit a phone, so they stand in for it; the full data list stays
       for screen readers. */
    .frontier-wrap { display: none; }
    .q-tune { grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin-top: 10px; }
    .who { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>

{# One palette for every engine — what it blocks at its default, solid and anchored
   left; then, pale, what its loosest setting adds (the suspicious band: counted for
   no engine, but part of each engine's story, and named at the end of the row);
   a grey tail on the right for what the engine never takes — a file format or an
   ecosystem it does not read — which the methodology scores as a miss. Atomdrift is identified by its label, not by a colour of its own. #}
{%- macro rows(board, cohort, full, eco) -%}
  <div class="rows">
  {%- for s in board | byFlagged %}
    {%- set p = providers[s.scanner] %}
    {%- set unsup = s.unsupported or 0 %}
    {#- The suspicious band and the setting range come from the operating points
        of the same cohort: the whole window, or this ecosystem's. -#}
    {%- set rng = battle | settingRange(s.scanner, eco) %}
    <div class="rn{% if s.scanner == 'ascan' %} us{% endif %}">{{ p.name or s.scanner }}</div>
    <div class="tr" role="img" aria-label="{{ p.name or s.scanner }}: {{ s.hostile }} blocked{% if rng %} at {{ rng.defSetting }}, {{ rng.extra }} more at {{ rng.looseSetting }}{% endif %}{% if s.nodata %}, {{ s.nodata }} no record{% endif %}{% if s.errored %}, {{ s.errored }} errored{% endif %}{% if unsup %}, {{ unsup }} out of scope{% endif %}, of {{ s.supported }}" title="{{ s.hostile }} blocked{% if rng %} at {{ rng.defSetting }} · {{ rng.extra }} more at {{ rng.looseSetting }}{% endif %} · of {{ s.supported }}{% if s.nodata %} · {{ s.nodata }} no record{% endif %}{% if s.errored %} · {{ s.errored }} errored{% endif %}{% if unsup %} · {{ unsup }} out of scope{% endif %}">
      {%- if s.supported > 0 -%}
        {%- if s.hostile > 0 %}<span class="hb" style="width:{{ s.hostile / s.supported * 100 }}%"></span>{% endif -%}
        {%- if rng %}<span class="sb" style="width:{{ rng.extra / s.supported * 100 }}%"></span>{% endif -%}
        {%- if unsup > 0 %}<span class="un" style="width:{{ unsup / s.supported * 100 }}%"></span>{% endif -%}
        {#- The red segment names its own casualties: which samples the engine
            failed to read, and what it said. Its own title beats the row's. -#}
        {%- if s.errored > 0 %}{% set errs = (battle.samples | errorLines(s.scanner, cohort)) if full else [] %}<span class="eb" style="width:{{ s.errored / s.supported * 100 }}%" role="img" aria-label="{{ p.name or s.scanner }} errored on {{ s.errored }} sample{{ 's' if s.errored != 1 }}: {{ errs | join('; ') }}" title="errored on {{ s.errored }} sample{{ 's' if s.errored != 1 }}
{%- for l in errs %}
{{ l }}
{%- endfor %}"></span>{% endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- if s.supported %}
    {#- The cell shows the rate over this cohort. The tooltip adds the same rate
        re-weighted onto the format population the cohort was drawn from, because
        the cohort is deliberately not proportional to it — see the appendix. -#}
    <div class="rv"{% if s.weighted_hostile_rate %} title="{{ (100 * s.hostile / s.supported) | pct1 }}% over this cohort · {{ (100 * s.weighted_hostile_rate) | pct1 }}% weighted to the format population"{% endif %}>{{ (100 * s.hostile / s.supported) | pct1 }}%{% if rng %} <span class="rs">({{ rng.defSetting }}) to {{ rng.looseDet | pct1 }}% ({{ rng.looseSetting }})</span>{% endif %}</div>
    {%- else %}
    <div class="rv" style="color:var(--slate)">—</div>
    {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  </div>
{%- endmacro -%}

<div class="main-full compare">

  {%- set h = battle | headline %}
  {#- battle.json is the published window: every sample scored over the last
      battle.window.days, scored as one cohort. Every figure on this page reads it
      except the trend chart, which is per-run by design. -#}
  {%- set span = ("the last " ~ battle.window.days ~ " days") if battle.window else "this run" %}
  {%- set curve = battle | ascanDial %}

  <div class="cmp-hero">
    <div>
      {#- The claim is the like-for-like number: Atomdrift at the -l whose
          false-positive rate matches the strongest rival's default, against that
          rival. Generated from the data, so it steps down when the data does. -#}
      {%- set rival = providers[h.parity.rival].name if h and h.parity else null %}
      {%- if h and h.parity and h.parity.det > h.parity.rivalDet %}
      <h1>More zero-day malware blocked than {{ rival }}, at the same false-positive rate — on your own
        hardware.</h1>
      <p class="say">Over {{ span }}, set to <code>-l {{ h.parity.level }}</code>: <b>{{ h.parity.det | pct1 }}%</b> of
        live zero-day malware blocked at <b>{{ h.parity.fp | pct1 }}%</b> false positives. {{ rival }} blocked
        {{ h.parity.rivalDet | pct1 }}%, one upload at a time. Atomdrift reads the artifact and decides at scan time;
        nothing leaves your machine. The shipped default, <code>-l {{ dialDefault }}</code>, is beside it.</p>
      {%- else %}
      <h1>Zero-day malware detection on your own hardware.</h1>
      <p class="say">Most engines ask whether anyone has reported a file yet. Atomdrift reads it and decides at scan
        time, and nothing leaves your machine. Measured every day against live malware under 48 hours old.</p>
      {%- endif %}
      {# One action. The install line is the call to action; everything else on the
         page is reached by scrolling, so it gets no button. #}
      <div class="instl">curl -fsSL https://install.atomdrift.org/scan.sh | sh</div>
      <p class="facts">Apache-2.0 · Linux, macOS, Windows, BSD, illumos · no telemetry</p>
    </div>

    {%- if h %}
    <div class="proof">
      {# The window pools the last few days of runs: one 50-sample night moves a
         false-positive rate two points per verdict, which is noise, not the
         engine. The per-run numbers are on the bars and the trend chart below. #}
      {%- if h.window %}
      <div class="l win">Last {{ h.window.days }} days · {{ h.window.runs }} runs</div>
      {%- endif %}
      <div class="scores">
        {# "0-day" is the whole claim: signatures and reputation have had no time to
           form on a package published this morning, which is exactly the window a
           supply-chain attack lives in. The cohort line below defines it. #}
        <div><div class="n">{{ h.detRate | pct1 }}%</div><div class="l">0-day malware detected</div></div>
        {%- if h.fpRate != null %}
        <div><div class="n fp">{{ h.fpRate | pct1 }}%</div><div class="l">false positives</div></div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- if curve %}
      {%- set dialStop = curve | curveStop(dialDefault) %}
      {# Server-rendered at the shipped default, so the numbers above are right with
         JS off; the slider only ever re-reads values already in the page, and moves
         Atomdrift's point on the chart below with it. #}
      <div class="dial">
        <label class="dial-label" for="dial">False-positive budget</label>
        <input type="range" id="dial" min="0" max="{{ (curve | length) - 1 }}"
               value="{{ curve | curveIndex(dialDefault) }}" step="1"
               aria-valuetext="-l {{ dialStop.l }}: {{ dialStop.det | pct1 }}% detected, {{ dialStop.fp | pct1 }}% false positives"
               aria-describedby="dial-help">
        <div class="ends"><span>-l {{ (curve | first).l }}</span><span>-l {{ (curve | last).l | int }}</span></div>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      <div class="at" id="dial-help">at <b id="dial-l">-l {{ dialDefault }}</b> <span id="dial-say">— the shipped default, untuned</span></div>
      <span id="dial-status" class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span>
      <p>Blocked as hostile · {{ h.sampleCount }} zero-day samples, median
        {{ battle.malware_age.median_hours | round(0) if battle.malware_age else 24 }} h old · {{ h.nGood }} known-good ·
        through {{ battle.generated_at | dateDisplay }}</p>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>

  {%- set ecos = battle.detection.by_ecosystem | byEcoSize %}
  <h2 id="results">Detected, per engine <span class="note">{{ span }} · identical cohort</span>
    {#- One board per ecosystem, switched by the dropdown; without script the
        page is the whole cohort. Small ecosystems are listed with their count
        so a 2-of-2 reads as what it is. -#}
    <label class="eco-pick">Ecosystem
      <select id="eco-pick" aria-controls="boards">
        <option value="all">All · {{ battle.detection.sample_count }}</option>
        {%- for e in ecos %}<option value="{{ e.eco }}">{{ e.eco }} · {{ e.n }}</option>{% endfor %}
      </select></label></h2>
  <div id="boards">
    <div class="board" data-eco="all">{{ rows(battle.detection.leaderboard, 'bad', true) }}</div>
    {%- for e in ecos %}
    <div class="board" data-eco="{{ e.eco }}" hidden>{{ rows(e.board, 'bad', false, e.eco) }}</div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  <script>
  (function () {
    const pick = document.getElementById('eco-pick');
    if (!pick) return;
    pick.addEventListener('change', function () {
      document.querySelectorAll('#boards .board, .qwrap').forEach(function (b) { b.hidden = b.dataset.eco !== pick.value; });
    });
  })();
  </script>
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i class="hostile-key"></i>blocked at the default</span>
    <span><i class="suspicious-key"></i>suspicious <small>· more at the loosest setting, not counted</small></span>
    <span><i class="unsupported-key"></i>out of scope <small>· a miss</small></span>
    <span><i class="errored-key"></i>errored <small>· a miss</small></span>
  </div>

  {%- set cov = battle | blindSpots(providers) %}
  {%- set gap = (cov.rows | selectattr("hosted") | sort(true, false, "lookups") | first) if cov else null %}
  {%- set vt = battle.detection.leaderboard | find("scanner", "virustotal") %}
  <p class="vs"><b>Reputation lookups</b> (Socket, Aikido, SafeDep) answer whether a package has been reported.{% if cov %}
    {{ cov.nonPackage }} of {{ span }}' {{ cov.cohort }} samples weren't registry packages at all{% if gap %}; of the
    {{ gap.lookups }} {{ gap.name }} could look up, it had a record for {{ gap.lookups - gap.noRecord }}{% endif %}.{% endif %}
    Atomdrift reads the artifact, so a package published this morning, a firmware image or your own code gets the
    same verdict.</p>
  <p class="vs"><b>VirusTotal</b> is dozens of engines voting, one upload at a time: its public API allows four lookups
    a minute and five hundred a day.{% if vt and vt.supported %} On {{ span }}' zero-days it blocked
    {{ (100 * vt.hostile / vt.supported) | pct1 }}%.{% endif %} Atomdrift runs at the speed of your cores, with no
    quota and no upload. <a class="lnk" href="/scan/how-it-works/">How it decides →</a></p>

  <div class="diffs">
    <div><b>Runs on your cores.</b> Local, CPU-only, air-gapped if you like. No per-query bill, no rate limit, no
      upload: every core you add is throughput you own.</div>
    <div><b>Reads 100+ formats.</b> Source in every major language, ELF, PE, Mach-O, firmware, containers, archives,
      documents; packages from {{ providers.ascan.registries | length }} registries.</div>
    <div><b>Built to be embedded.</b> Exit codes, JSON, an HTTP service, Rust libraries. Apache-2.0: ship it inside
      what you sell.</div>
  </div>

{#- The chart, its sliders and its data list, for one cohort: the whole window,
    or one ecosystem. Rendered once per ecosystem and switched by the dropdown in
    "Detected, per engine"; without script the page is the whole cohort. -#}
{%- macro frontier(q, span) -%}
  <div class="frontier-wrap">
    <svg class="qchart" viewBox="0 0 {{ q.w }} {{ q.h }}" role="img" aria-label="Zero-day malware blocked against known-good files blocked, for every engine over {{ span }}, each at its default setting. Faded dots are the other settings an engine can run at. The vertical axis is inverted so fewer false positives is higher. Every value follows the chart in a list.">
      {# The one shaded region on the chart: high detection, few false positives. #}
      <rect class="q-target" x="{{ q.xDiv }}" y="{{ q.pt }}" width="{{ q.pr - q.xDiv }}" height="{{ q.yDiv - q.pt }}"></rect>
      <rect class="q-target-edge" x="{{ q.xDiv }}" y="{{ q.pt }}" width="{{ q.pr - q.xDiv }}" height="{{ q.yDiv - q.pt }}"></rect>

      {%- for t in q.xTicks %}
      <line class="q-grid" x1="{{ t.x }}" y1="{{ q.pt }}" x2="{{ t.x }}" y2="{{ q.pb }}"></line>
      <text class="q-tick" x="{{ t.x }}" y="{{ q.pb + 20 }}" text-anchor="middle">{{ t.v }}%</text>
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- for t in q.yTicks %}
      <line class="q-grid" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ t.y }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ t.y }}"></line>
      <text class="q-tick" x="{{ q.pl - 9 }}" y="{{ t.y + 4 }}" text-anchor="end">{{ t.v }}%</text>
      {%- endfor %}
      <line class="q-div" x1="{{ q.xDiv }}" y1="{{ q.pt }}" x2="{{ q.xDiv }}" y2="{{ q.mb }}"></line>
      <line class="q-div" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.yDiv }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ q.yDiv }}"></line>
      <text class="q-quad" x="{{ q.pr - 10 }}" y="{{ q.yDiv - 10 }}" text-anchor="end">HIGH DETECTION  ·  LOW FALSE POSITIVES</text>

      <line class="q-axis" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.pt }}" x2="{{ q.pl }}" y2="{{ q.pb }}"></line>
      <line class="q-axis" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.pb }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ q.pb }}"></line>
      <text class="q-alab" x="{{ (q.pl + q.pr) / 2 }}" y="{{ q.pb + 46 }}" text-anchor="middle">Zero-day malware blocked  ·  more is better →</text>
      <text class="q-asub" x="{{ (q.pl + q.pr) / 2 }}" y="{{ q.pb + 62 }}" text-anchor="middle">of {{ q.nBad }} malicious packages{% if q.window %} across {{ q.window.runs }} runs{% endif %}, none more than 48 hours old</text>
      <g transform="translate(24,{{ (q.pt + q.pb) / 2 }}) rotate(-90)">
        <text class="q-alab" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="middle">False positives  ·  fewer is better ↑</text>
        <text class="q-asub" x="0" y="15" text-anchor="middle">of {{ q.nGood }} known-safe packages</text>
      </g>

      {# Settings first, so every coloured point and label sits on top of them. #}
      {%- for e in q.engines %}{% if e.line %}<polyline class="q-line" points="{{ e.line }}" stroke="{{ e.color }}"></polyline>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {%- for e in q.engines %}
      <g class="q-eng" data-key="{{ e.key }}">
        {%- if e.tuned %}
        {%- for o in e.optsView %}{% if o.onPlot %}
        <circle class="q-opt{% if o.isDefault %} on{% endif %}" cx="{{ o.x }}" cy="{{ o.y }}" r="5" tabindex="0" role="button"
          fill="{{ e.color }}" stroke="{{ e.color }}"
          aria-label="{{ o.title }}" data-x="{{ o.x }}" data-y="{{ o.y }}" data-level="{{ o.level }}" data-idx="{{ o.idx }}"
          data-rates="{{ o.rates }}" data-setting="{{ o.setting }}"
          data-lx="{{ o.label.tx }}" data-ly="{{ o.label.y }}" data-anchor="{{ o.label.anchor }}"
          {%- if o.label.leader %} data-leader="{{ o.label.leader.x1 }},{{ o.label.leader.y1 }},{{ o.label.leader.x2 }},{{ o.label.leader.y2 }}"{% endif %}><title>{{ o.title }}</title></circle>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
        {%- endif %}
        <g class="q-move">
          {#- Always present, so a setting that needs a leader can show one. -#}
          <line class="q-leader" x1="{{ e.leader.x1 if e.leader else 0 }}" y1="{{ e.leader.y1 if e.leader else 0 }}" x2="{{ e.leader.x2 if e.leader else 0 }}" y2="{{ e.leader.y2 if e.leader else 0 }}"{% if not e.leader %} visibility="hidden"{% endif %}></line>
          <circle class="q-pt" cx="{{ e.x }}" cy="{{ e.y }}" r="{{ 6 if e.us else 5 }}" fill="{{ e.color }}"><title>{{ e.title }}</title></circle>
          <text class="q-lab" x="{{ e.label.tx }}" y="{{ e.label.y }}" text-anchor="{{ e.label.anchor }}"><tspan class="q-lname">{{ e.name }}</tspan><tspan class="q-rates" dx="7">{{ e.rates }}</tspan>{% if e.setting %}<tspan class="q-setting" dx="7">{{ e.setting }}</tspan>{% endif %}</text>
        </g>
      </g>
      {%- endfor %}

      {# Settings past the crop sit in a strip below an axis break, at their true
         detection rate, their false-positive rate in their label. #}
      {%- if q.strip %}
      <line class="q-grid" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.strip.breakY }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ q.strip.breakY }}"></line>
      <line class="q-break-mask" x1="{{ q.pl - 6 }}" y1="{{ q.strip.breakY + 8 }}" x2="{{ q.pl + 5 }}" y2="{{ q.strip.breakY - 8 }}"></line>
      <line class="q-break" x1="{{ q.pl - 6 }}" y1="{{ q.strip.breakY + 8 }}" x2="{{ q.pl + 5 }}" y2="{{ q.strip.breakY - 8 }}"></line>
      <text class="q-tick" x="{{ q.pl - 9 }}" y="{{ q.strip.y + 4 }}" text-anchor="end">&gt;{{ q.yMax }}%</text>
      {%- endif %}
    </svg>
  </div>
  {#- One slider per engine with settings to choose from, strictest to loosest. It
      and the chart's dots drive the same selection. -#}
  <div class="q-tune">
    {%- for e in q.engines %}{% if e.tuned %}
    {%- set d = e.slider[e.sliderDefault] %}
    <label class="q-knob" data-key="{{ e.key }}">
      <span class="q-kname" style="--c: {{ e.color }}">{{ e.name }}</span>
      <input type="range" min="0" max="{{ (e.slider | length) - 1 }}" value="{{ e.sliderDefault }}" step="1"
        aria-valuetext="{{ d.setting }}: {{ d.rates }}">
      <span class="q-kval"><b>{{ d.setting }}</b> {{ d.rates }}</span>
    </label>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="visually-hidden q-data">
    <h3>Detection and false-positive chart data</h3>
    <ul>
      {%- for e in q.engines %}{% for o in e.optsView %}<li>{{ o.title }}{% if o.isDefault and e.tuned %} (default){% endif %}.</li>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
{%- endmacro -%}

  {%- set q = battle | quadrant(chartProviders) %}
  {%- if q %}
  <h2 id="frontier">Detection vs. false positives <span class="note">{{ span }} · sliders try each engine's other settings</span></h2>
  <div class="qwrap" data-eco="all">{{ frontier(q, span) }}</div>
  {%- for e in ecos %}
  {%- set qe = (battle | quadrant(chartProviders, e.eco)) if e.n >= 10 else null %}
  <div class="qwrap" data-eco="{{ e.eco }}" hidden>
    {%- if qe %}{{ frontier(qe, span) }}
    {%- else %}<p class="fig-note q-none">{{ e.eco }}: {% if e.n < 10 %}{{ e.n }} malware sample{{ 's' if e.n != 1 }} in {{ span }} is too few to chart{% else %}no known-good files of this kind in {{ span }}, so no false-positive rate to plot{% endif %}. The bars above still show it.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endfor %}
  <p class="fig-note">Detection is what each engine blocks as hostile; suspicious verdicts count for no engine.
    Defaults: Atomdrift <code>L25</code> (as shipped), VirusTotal <code>n=4</code> engines agreeing, GuardDog
    <code>risk≥7</code> (its "likely malicious"), malcontent <code>critical</code>.</p>
  <script>
  (function () {
    // Selecting a faded dot moves its engine's point there, with the label at the
    // spot laid out for that setting when the page was built. One chart per
    // ecosystem; each is wired on its own. window.qSelect lets the hero's dial
    // drive Atomdrift's point on every chart.
    const charts = [];
    document.querySelectorAll('.qwrap').forEach(function (wrap) {
      const svg = wrap.querySelector('svg.qchart');
      if (!svg) return;
      const groups = {};
      svg.querySelectorAll('.q-eng').forEach(function (g) {
        const opts = g.querySelectorAll('.q-opt');
        if (!opts.length) return;
        const dot = g.querySelector('.q-move .q-pt'), lab = g.querySelector('.q-lab'), leader = g.querySelector('.q-leader');
        const rates = lab.querySelector('.q-rates'), set = lab.querySelector('.q-setting');
        const knob = wrap.querySelector('.q-knob[data-key="' + g.dataset.key + '"]');
        function select(o) {
          const d = o.dataset;
          dot.setAttribute('cx', d.x);
          dot.setAttribute('cy', d.y);
          lab.setAttribute('x', d.lx);
          lab.setAttribute('y', d.ly);
          lab.setAttribute('text-anchor', d.anchor);
          rates.textContent = d.rates;
          if (set) set.textContent = d.setting;
          if (d.leader) {
            const [x1, y1, x2, y2] = d.leader.split(',');
            leader.setAttribute('x1', x1); leader.setAttribute('y1', y1);
            leader.setAttribute('x2', x2); leader.setAttribute('y2', y2);
            leader.removeAttribute('visibility');
          } else {
            leader.setAttribute('visibility', 'hidden');
          }
          opts.forEach(function (p) { p.classList.toggle('on', p === o); });
          if (knob) {
            knob.querySelector('input').value = d.idx;
            knob.querySelector('input').setAttribute('aria-valuetext', d.setting + ': ' + d.rates);
            knob.querySelector('.q-kval').innerHTML = '<b>' + d.setting + '</b> ' + d.rates;
          }
        }
        opts.forEach(function (o) {
          o.addEventListener('click', function () { select(o); });
          o.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
            if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); select(o); }
          });
        });
        groups[g.dataset.key] = { opts: opts, select: select };
        if (knob) knob.querySelector('input').addEventListener('input', function () {
          const o = [...opts].find(function (p) { return p.dataset.idx === knob.querySelector('input').value; });
          if (!o) return;
          select(o);
          // Atomdrift's slider and the hero's dial are one control.
          if (g.dataset.key === 'ascan' && window.heroSet) window.heroSet(+o.dataset.level);
        });
      });
      charts.push(groups);
    });
    window.qSelect = function (key, level) {
      charts.forEach(function (groups) {
        const g = groups[key];
        if (g) g.opts.forEach(function (o) { if (+o.dataset.level === level) g.select(o); });
      });
    };
  })();
  </script>
  {%- endif %}

  <h2 id="over-time">Every previous run <span class="note">last 30 days · a fresh cohort each time</span></h2>
  <p class="sub">A fresh cohort every run, so every line swings. <span id="trend-n"></span> <b>Judge us on the worst
    night, not the best.</b></p>
  {%- if history and history | length >= 2 %}
  <div class="trend-wrap"><canvas id="trendChart" role="img" aria-label="Per-run 0-day detection rate (blocked as hostile) for every measured engine across fresh live-malware cohorts."></canvas></div>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
  <script>
  (function () {
    // Rolling 30-day window so the chart stays focused on recent cohorts. Keep
    // the latest two valid points when the page is viewed after a long outage
    // or when a clock skew makes the rolling window sparse; Chart.js cannot
    // draw a line from an empty/single-point history series.
    const ALL = ({{ history | trendPoints | dump | safe }})
      .filter(p => p && Number.isFinite(Date.parse(p.at)))
      .sort((a, b) => Date.parse(a.at) - Date.parse(b.at));
    const CUTOFF = Date.now() - 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
    let H = ALL.filter(p => Date.parse(p.at) >= CUTOFF);
    if (H.length < 2) H = ALL.slice(-2);
    // A one-point history is still possible with a newly initialized site.
    // Duplicate it at the next hour so the measured value renders as a visible
    // degenerate line instead of disappearing entirely.
    if (H.length === 1) {
      const next = new Date(Date.parse(H[0].at) + 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();
      H = [H[0], Object.assign({}, H[0], { at: next })];
    }
    const tn = document.getElementById('trend-n');
    if (tn) tn.textContent = H.length + ' runs, ' +
      H.reduce((n, p) => n + (p.bad || 0), 0).toLocaleString('en-US') + ' samples.';
    const PROV = {{ chartProviders | dump | safe }};
    // Engine colors and draw order come from providers.json — one declaration
    // shared with the quadrant, so an engine keeps its hue across the page and
    // no engine can be missing from this chart just by being absent from a map
    // hardcoded here.
    const ENGINES = Object.keys(PROV).filter(e => !PROV[e].hidden)
      .sort((a, b) => (PROV[a].slot || 99) - (PROV[b].slot || 99));
    const COLOR = Object.fromEntries(ENGINES.map(e => [e, PROV[e].color || '#6b7280']));
    const US = 'ascan';
    const labels = H.map(p => new Date(p.at).toLocaleString(undefined, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', hour: 'numeric' }));
    // Atomdrift is the subject: drawn last (on top) and heavier than the field.
    // The emphasis is weight only — fading the others toward the surface used to
    // collapse them into each other (seven lines at 45% alpha sit ~7 ΔE apart,
    // under the ~15 a full-color reader needs), so every line keeps its own hue.
    const order = ENGINES.filter(e => e !== US).concat(US);
    const datasets = order.map(e => {
      const us = e === US;
      return {
        label: (PROV[e] && (PROV[e].chartName || PROV[e].name)) || e,
        data: H.map(p => (p.detection && p.detection[e] != null) ? Math.round(p.detection[e] * 100) : null),
        solidColor: COLOR[e],
        borderColor: COLOR[e],
        backgroundColor: COLOR[e],
        borderWidth: us ? 4 : 2,
        pointRadius: us ? 4 : 2.5,
        pointHoverRadius: us ? 6 : 4,
        tension: 0.25, spanGaps: true
      };
    }).filter(d => d.data.some(v => v != null));

    // Each line's latest value, labelled at its right end so current standings read
    // without hovering; labels are nudged apart vertically when they'd collide.
    const endLabels = {
      id: 'endLabels',
      afterDatasetsDraw(chart) {
        const ctx = chart.ctx;
        const items = [];
        chart.data.datasets.forEach((ds, i) => {
          const meta = chart.getDatasetMeta(i);
          if (meta.hidden || !meta.data.length) return;
          for (let j = ds.data.length - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
            if (ds.data[j] != null) {
              items.push({ x: meta.data[j].x, y: meta.data[j].y, val: ds.data[j], color: ds.solidColor, bold: ds.borderWidth >= 3 });
              break;
            }
          }
        });
        items.sort((a, b) => a.y - b.y);
        // Ties share a label; the rest are nudged apart.
        const shown = items.filter((it, i) => !i || it.val !== items[i - 1].val);
        for (let i = 1; i < shown.length; i++) {
          if (shown[i].y - shown[i - 1].y < 13) shown[i].y = shown[i - 1].y + 13;
        }
        items.length = 0; items.push(...shown);
        ctx.save();
        ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';
        items.forEach(it => {
          ctx.font = (it.bold ? '700 ' : '600 ') + '11px system-ui, sans-serif';
          ctx.fillStyle = '#404040';
          ctx.fillText(it.val + '%', it.x + 7, it.y);
        });
        ctx.restore();
      }
    };

    new Chart(document.getElementById('trendChart'), {
      type: 'line',
      data: { labels, datasets },
      plugins: [endLabels],
      options: {
        responsive: true, maintainAspectRatio: false,
        interaction: { mode: 'index', intersect: false },
        layout: { padding: { right: 46, left: 6 } },
        scales: {
          y: { beginAtZero: true, max: 100, ticks: { callback: v => v + '%' }, title: { display: true, text: '0-day malware blocked' } }
        },
        plugins: {
          // Chart.js defaults to a 40px line-style box per entry, which pushes
          // eight engines onto three rows and eats the chart's height. Small
          // circular swatches keep the whole field on one or two rows.
          legend: {
            position: 'bottom',
            labels: {
              usePointStyle: true, pointStyle: 'circle', boxWidth: 8, boxHeight: 8, padding: 12, font: { size: 11 },
              // VirusTotal's engine count earns its width on a full-size chart, but
              // the eight entries only just fit one row — adding "[66 engines]" tips
              // them onto a second row once the canvas drops below ~730px, which
              // comes straight out of the plot's height. Under that, fall back to the
              // bare name: the count is still on the quadrant and the bars. Chart.js
              // regenerates labels on resize, so this re-evaluates as the page reflows.
              generateLabels(chart) {
                const items = Chart.defaults.plugins.legend.labels.generateLabels(chart);
                if (chart.width < 730) {
                  for (const it of items) it.text = it.text.replace(/ \[\d+ engines\]$/, '');
                }
                return items;
              }
            }
          },
          tooltip: {
            itemSort: (a, b) => b.parsed.y - a.parsed.y,
            callbacks: { label: c => `${c.dataset.label}: ${c.parsed.y}%` }
          }
        }
      }
    });
  })();
  </script>
  {%- else %}
  <div class="meth">History is still collecting. Each run adds a point; the chart appears at two.</div>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if battle.fp_by_filetype and battle.fp_by_filetype.sample_n %}
  {%- set fpft = battle.fp_by_filetype %}
  <h2 id="fp-filetypes">False positives <span class="note">last {{ fpft.window_days }} days</span></h2>
  {%- set fps = fpft.false_positives or [] %}
  <p class="sub">Of {{ h.nGood if h else fpft.sample_n }} known-good artifacts, {{ h.fpFlagged or "none" }} blocked
    as hostile{% if h and h.fpFlagged %} ({{ h.fpRate | pct1 }}%),
    each linked to its report{% endif %}.</p>
  {%- if fps | length %}
  <table class="fpt">
    <thead><tr><th>File type</th><th>Flagged</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {%- for type, items in fps | groupby("filetype") %}
      <tr><td>{{ type }}</td><td>
        {%- for fp in items %}<a href="https://lab.isotope13.io/file/{{ fp.sha256 }}"
          title="{% if fp.ecosystem %}{{ fp.ecosystem }} · {% endif %}flagged {{ fp.tier }}"
          class="fp{{ fp.tier }}">{{ fp.name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endif %}

  {%- set badSamples = battle.samples | where("label", "bad") -%}
  {%- set cohortBad = badSamples | whereUnset("excluded") -%}
  {%- if curve %}
  <script>
  (function () {
    // One stop per -l, scored over the same samples as the chart: what Atomdrift
    // blocks at that level, and the false positives that costs. Moving the dial
    // moves Atomdrift's point on the chart too.
    const C = {{ curve | dump | safe }}, DEF = {{ dialDefault }};
    const el = document.getElementById('dial');
    if (!el || !C.length) return;
    const det = document.querySelector('.proof .n'), fp = document.querySelector('.proof .n.fp');
    const lab = document.getElementById('dial-l'), say = document.getElementById('dial-say');
    const status = document.getElementById('dial-status');
    const p1 = (v) => v.toFixed(1) + '%';
    const stance = (l) => l === DEF ? '— the shipped default, untuned'
      : (l === 0 ? '— zero false-positive budget' : (l < DEF ? '— stricter than the default' : '— tuned for recall'));
    const say1 = (c) => '-l ' + c.l.toLocaleString('en-US') + ': ' + p1(c.det) + ' detected, ' + p1(c.fp) + ' false positives';
    function render() {
      const c = C[+el.value];
      if (det) det.textContent = p1(c.det);
      if (fp) fp.textContent = p1(c.fp);
      lab.textContent = '-l ' + c.l.toLocaleString('en-US');
      say.textContent = stance(c.l);
      el.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', say1(c));
      if (window.qSelect) window.qSelect('ascan', c.l);
    }
    // The chart's Atomdrift slider drives this dial too.
    window.heroSet = function (level) {
      const i = C.findIndex(function (c) { return c.l === level; });
      if (i >= 0 && +el.value !== i) { el.value = i; render(); }
    };
    el.addEventListener('input', render);
    el.addEventListener('change', function () {
      if (status) status.textContent = say1(C[+el.value]);
    });
    render();
  })();
  </script>
  {%- endif %}

  <p class="hosted">Rules the hour they clear QA, an API, and someone on the hook:
    <a href="https://isotope13.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">isotope13.io</a>.</p>

  <details class="appendix" id="samples">
    <summary>Appendix — samples and methodology <span class="note">all {{ cohortBad | length }}, every one linked</span></summary>
  <div class="samples">
    {%- for sm in cohortBad | sort(false, false, "filename") %}
    <a href="https://lab.atomdrift.org/file/{{ sm.sha256 }}" title="{{ sm.filename }}{% if sm.ecosystem %} · {{ sm.ecosystem }}{% endif %} — view in Atomdrift Lab">{{ sm.purl or sm.filename }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="meth"><b>What “0-day” means here.</b> Every detection sample first appeared in the wild less than 48
    hours before the run{% if battle.malware_age %} (median {{ battle.malware_age.median_hours | round(0) }} h, youngest
    {{ battle.malware_age.min_hours | round(1) }} h){% endif %}: no signature written for it, no reputation, no
    download history to be anomalous against. Catching malware a feed has already named is a different, easier problem.
    <br><br><b>How this is scored.</b> Every engine gets the identical cohort at its most sensitive setting, and a
    skip counts as a miss for everyone — a file nobody scanned is a file that got through. A listing from a contestant's own feed counts only
    once an independent engine corroborates it. Known-good packages come from the freshest 48 hours of the open-source
    firehose and are re-checked later: one that turns out to be malware is dropped from that run's false-positive
    rates, and any engine that flagged it is credited with an early detection.
    <b>We run this benchmark and we're one of the engines in it</b>, so we publish every sample, verdict and rate.
    {%- if battle.versions %}
    <br><br><b>Engine versions:</b> {% for k, v in battle.versions %}{% if not loop.first %} · {% endif %}{{ providers[k].name or k }} {{ v }}{% endfor %}
    <span style="color:var(--slate)">(locally run engines; {% for p in providers | bySlot | selectattr("hosted") %}{{ p.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} are hosted services queried live, so they carry no pinned version).</span>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  {%- set dw = battle.detection.weighting %}
  {%- set fw = battle.false_positive.weighting %}
  {%- if dw %}
  <div class="meth"><b>Why the cohort isn't a random sample.</b> A plain random draw from the malware and open-source
    firehoses is dominated by whatever published most: three registries took 70% of the known-good seats and Windows
    executables 60% of the malware seats, which left most file formats never measured at all. So each cohort is built
    from two parts. Most seats track the real population, damped by a square root so the biggest format stays the
    biggest without crowding out everything else. The rest go one-per-format on a rotation, and that rotation is the
    only reason a Firefox add-on or a Conda package appears here at all.
    {%- if battle.detection.strata_count and battle.detection.strata_count.breadth %}
    Over {{ span }}: {{ battle.detection.strata_count.fairness or 0 }} proportional seats and
    {{ battle.detection.strata_count.breadth or 0 }} rotation seats on the malware side, across
    {{ dw.classes | length }} formats.
    {%- endif %}
    <br><br><b>So every rate is published twice.</b> The percentage in the table is the rate over this cohort. Because
    the cohort over-samples rare formats deliberately, that is not what an engine would score on the population — so
    each rate is also re-weighted by every format's true share of it. Hover a percentage to see both.
    {#- Every engine, not selectattr: a weighted rate of exactly 0 is falsy, and
        dropping an engine that scored 0% would read as it not being measured. -#}
    <br><br><b>Weighted to the population:</b>
    {%- for s in battle.detection.leaderboard %}{% if not loop.first %} · {% endif %}{{ providers[s.scanner].name or s.scanner }}
      {{ (100 * (s.weighted_hostile_rate or 0)) | pct1 }}%{% endfor %}.
    {%- if dw.population_covered < 0.999 %}
    <br><br><span style="color:var(--slate)">The weighted malware rates speak for
      {{ (100 * dw.population_covered) | round(0) }}% of the population: nothing was drawn over {{ span }} for
      {{ dw.unseated_classes | join(', ') }}.</span>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if fw and fw.population_covered < 0.999 %}
    <br><br><span style="color:var(--slate)">On the false-positive side they speak for
      {{ (100 * fw.population_covered) | round(0) }}%: nothing was drawn for {{ fw.unseated_classes | join(', ') }}.</span>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- set lead = battle.detection.leaderboard | first %}
    {%- if lead and lead.effective_n %}
    <br><br><span style="color:var(--slate)">Re-weighting costs precision, so here is the cost: these
      {{ battle.detection.sample_count }} malware samples carry the statistical weight of
      {{ lead.effective_n | round(0) }} once weighted. A cohort spread across many formats is less precise about any
      one of them than the same cohort spent on a single format.</span>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
  </details>

  <div class="closer">
    <div>
      <h3>Point it at anything.</h3>
      <p>Apache-2.0 · runs locally · no account, no index, no gap</p>
    </div>
    <div class="inst">curl -fsSL https://install.atomdrift.org/scan.sh | sh</div>
  </div>

</div>
